  "guidebook": {
    "intro": "Buses, trains and planes connect the towns of East Africa. Here you’ll plan a journey and learn to talk about the future.",
    "phrases": [
      { "target": "Tiketi ni bei gani?", "base": "How much is the ticket?" },
      { "target": "Nitasafiri kesho.", "base": "I will travel tomorrow." },
      { "target": "Utasafiri lini?", "base": "When will you travel?" },
      { "target": "Tutaondoka mapema.", "base": "We will leave early." },
      { "target": "Nimechelewa! Samahani.", "base": "I’m late! Sorry." },
      { "target": "Safari njema!", "base": "Have a good trip!" }
    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "ta-future",
        "title": "The future: -ta-",
        "body": [
          "Put **-ta-** where **-na-** was and you are talking about the future: **ninasafiri** (I’m travelling) becomes **nitasafiri** (I will travel). Notice **nina-** shortens to **ni-**.",
          "It works for everyone: **utasafiri** (you will), **tutaondoka** (we will leave), **treni itafika** (the train will arrive). Ask when with **lini** at the end: **Utasafiri lini?**"
        ],
        "table": [["Now", "Future"], ["ninasafiri", "nitasafiri"], ["tunaondoka", "tutaondoka"], ["inafika", "itafika"]],
        "targetColumns": [0, 1]
      },
      {
        "id": "ji-ma",
        "title": "Gari and its friends",
        "body": [
          "Some nouns have no prefix in the singular and **ma-** in the plural: **gari, magari**; **jibu, majibu**; **swali, maswali**. Their describing words take **ji-** or **l-**: **gari langu jipya** (my new car), **swali la tatu** (the third question).",
          "In the plural they all use **ma-** forms: **magari mapya**, **maswali yangu**."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Pole pole, but on time",
        "body": [
          "Long-distance buses leave when they are full, and a **matatu** may wait a while. Trains and planes do not: for those, **mapema** (early) is the rule."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
